# GitHub PR File Explorer Enhancer

Utility ideas and prototype code for improving GitHub pull request "Files changed" review flow.

## Mission

Add native-feeling quality-of-life controls to GitHub PR file review pages:

1. Locate the currently viewed diff file in GitHub's file explorer.
2. Jump quickly back to the top of the PR files page.
3. Optional: copy editor commands for Cursor or VS Code.
4. Later: explore sticky working-file tabs and comment-flow helpers.

## Stack

- TypeScript 5
- Vite 5 + `@crxjs/vite-plugin`
- Manifest V3 Chrome extension
- Vanilla DOM content script (no framework) for the GitHub page
- React + Tailwind + shadcn-ui for the toolbar popup
- Tiny vanilla options page for editor command settings

## Layout

```text
manifest.json                # MV3 manifest, source-of-truth for crxjs
vite.config.ts
tsconfig.json
src/
  content/
    main.ts                  # entry, orchestrates init() + observer
    enhanceFileHeaders.ts    # injects locate (+ optional editor) buttons
    observeGitHubUpdates.ts  # debounced MutationObserver
    goToTopButton.ts
  features/
    locate/                  # P0: locate file in explorer
    editor/                  # P2: editor command, gated by setting
    fileTabs/                # IDE-like preview/permanent tabs for active review files
    reviewFlow/              # comment navigation, context copy, comment badges
  shared/
    settings.ts              # single source of truth for chrome.storage settings
    diagnostics.ts           # guarded debug logging and safe feature wrappers
    tooltip.ts, icons.ts, dom.ts, buttonFactory.ts, stickyHeader.ts, constants.ts
  styles/content.css         # injected on PR pages
  popup/                     # React + Tailwind + shadcn quick-toggle popup
  components/ui/             # shadcn ui primitives (switch, label, button, segmented, separator)
  lib/utils.ts               # cn() helper
  options/                   # settings UI for the editor command
```

## Develop

Install dependencies once:

```bash
npm install
```

Dev mode with HMR (Vite writes to `dist/`, Chrome reloads on change):

```bash
npm run dev
```

Production build:

```bash
npm run build
```

Type check only:

```bash
npm run typecheck
```

## Install As Unpacked Extension

If you just want to use the extension and aren't planning to dive into the code, follow the friendly walkthrough in [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md). It covers prerequisites, building, loading the unpacked extension, pinning the toolbar icon, updating to new versions, and a feature-by-feature usage guide.

Quick version for developers already familiar with the flow:

1. Run `npm run build` (or `npm run dev` for live reload).
2. Open `chrome://extensions`.
3. Enable Developer mode.
4. Click "Load unpacked".
5. Select the `dist/` folder in this repo (not the repo root).
6. Open or refresh a GitHub PR files page.

## Features

Toolbar popup (click the extension icon while on any page):

- Toggle the "locate file in explorer" icon on/off.
- Toggle IDE-like file tabs on/off.
- Toggle the review-flow rail on/off, plus each rail button individually.
- Toggle the floating back-to-top button on/off.
- Pick what plain click vs Shift-click does for back-to-top: jump to **Files top** or **Page top**, independently configurable.
- Swap the two with one click.

On a PR page, all on by default:

- Locate icon in each PR file diff header (placed after GitHub's "Copy file name to clipboard" button when available).
- Native-looking tooltip for the injected icon buttons.
- File path extracted from `data-file-path`, with `h3 code` fallback.
- File tree match in `#pr-file-tree`, scrolled as close to centered as scroll bounds allow, with a brief highlight pulse.
- Mutation observer keeps newly-rendered diff headers enhanced as GitHub paginates.
- Floating back-to-top button after scrolling down.
- IDE-like file tabs at the top of the diff view: single-click a file header to open an italic preview tab, double-click the file header or tab to keep it as a permanent tab, and click tabs to jump back to files.
- Pin icon in each file header for explicitly keeping or removing a permanent tab.
- Terminal icon that copies a `cursor -g` or `code -g` command for the file at the visible right-side line. The first click prompts for the local repo root.
- Compact review rail with previous/next comment, next unviewed file, and copy review context actions.
- Current-file comment status in the review rail.
- Subtle file-explorer dots for files with visible review comments.

## Current Feature Matrix

| Feature | Default | Control surface | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Locate file in explorer | On | Toolbar popup | Adds an icon to each file header and scrolls `#pr-file-tree` to the matching file. |
| File tabs | On | Toolbar popup | Adds an IDE-like tab row above the sticky file header; preview tabs are italic until double-clicked or pinned. |
| Back to top | On | Toolbar popup | Click and Shift-click targets are configurable. |
| Review flow rail | On | Toolbar popup | Previous/next comment, next unviewed file, copy review context, and current-file comment status. |
| Review rail buttons | On | Toolbar popup | Previous comment, next comment, next unviewed, and copy context can be shown or hidden independently. |
| Comment dots | On with review flow | Toolbar popup | Adds a subtle dot to files with visible review comments. |
| Editor command copy | On | Options page | First use prompts for repo root; direct editor opening is not implemented yet. |

## Settings

All settings live in `chrome.storage.local` under the `prFileExplorer.*` namespace. Two surfaces edit them:

- **Toolbar popup** — locate toggle, back-to-top toggle, click bindings.
- **Options page** — `chrome://extensions` → Details → Extension options. Editor command enable/disable, editor choice, local repo root.

Stored keys:

```text
prFileExplorer.locateEnabled
prFileExplorer.backToTopEnabled
prFileExplorer.backToTopClickAction         # "filesTop" | "pageTop"
prFileExplorer.backToTopShiftClickAction    # "filesTop" | "pageTop"
prFileExplorer.reviewFlowEnabled
prFileExplorer.reviewFlowPreviousCommentEnabled
prFileExplorer.reviewFlowNextCommentEnabled
prFileExplorer.reviewFlowNextUnviewedEnabled
prFileExplorer.reviewFlowCopyContextEnabled
prFileExplorer.fileTabsEnabled
prFileExplorer.editorEnabled
prFileExplorer.editor                       # "cursor" | "code"
prFileExplorer.repoRoot
```

The editor button is **enabled by default**, but it has no preconfigured `repoRoot`. The first time you click the terminal icon on a file header, you'll be prompted for the editor (`cursor` or `code`) and the local repository root, e.g. `~/Projects/your-repo`. After that the click silently copies the command.

You can also configure (or fully disable) it from the options page (`chrome://extensions` → Details → Extension options). Option-click the terminal icon on any PR page for an inline reconfigure prompt.

## Manual Test

1. Build and load the unpacked extension from `dist/`.
2. Open a GitHub PR files page.
3. Make sure the file explorer/sidebar is visible.
4. Click the locate icon in a file header.
5. Confirm the matching file tree item scrolls into view and flashes.
6. Scroll down. Confirm the back-to-top button appears.
7. Click it to jump to the top of the PR files area.
8. Shift-click for absolute page top.
9. Open the toolbar popup, swap the click and shift-click bindings, then test that the behavior flips.
10. Toggle the locate feature off in the popup and confirm the icons disappear from file headers.
11. (Optional) Enable the editor command icon in options, then click it on a file header and confirm a command like `cursor -g "/path/to/repo/file.ts:123"` is copied.
12. Use the review rail to jump to the previous or next comment, jump to the next unviewed file, or copy Markdown review context.
13. Confirm files with visible review threads get a subtle dot in the file explorer.
14. Single-click a file header and confirm it appears as an italic preview tab.
15. Single-click another file header and confirm the preview tab is replaced.
16. Double-click a file header or preview tab and confirm it becomes a permanent tab.
17. Pin several files, jump between them from the tab row, close one tab, and confirm the matching header pin state updates.

### Live PR QA Checklist

- Large PR: locate icon scrolls the file explorer correctly, back-to-top works, and floating controls do not cover GitHub review buttons.
- File tabs: preview tabs are italic and replaceable, double-click makes them permanent, tabs jump to the correct files, active tab follows scroll position, and closing a tab updates the header pin state.
- PR with comments: previous/next comment jumps through visible threads, current-file status changes while scrolling, and sidebar dots only appear on commented files.
- Viewed state: next unviewed enables when any file is `Not Viewed`, disables when none are visible, and lands on the expected file.
- File explorer states: visible, filtered, collapsed/missing, and duplicate basenames in different folders.
- Settings: review-flow toggle removes/restores the rail and dots; individual review rail button toggles hide/show only their buttons; locate and back-to-top toggles remove/restore their controls.

Debug logging can be enabled in the page console with:

```js
localStorage.setItem("prFileExplorer.debug", "true")
```

Reload the PR page after changing it. Debug output is console-only and never shown in the UI.

## Legacy Userscript

The original Tampermonkey-style userscript still lives at:

```text
src/github-pr-file-explorer.user.js
```

It is not used by the extension build any more, but it remains for users who prefer Tampermonkey or DevTools Snippets. The TypeScript content script is the source of truth going forward.

